<a name="postgresqllimitations"/><h1>Limitations</h1>

<p>The implementation of the PostgreSQL protocol is likely sufficient for most applications, but it isn't 100% complete.  Some notable limitations follow:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Kerberos authentication and encryption are not supported.</li>
  <li>Multi-statement queries are not supported.</li>
  <li>Result sets are always returned in text format, even if a client requests binary format.</li>
  <li>A binary-format bind parameter isn't supported for every type - date, time, timetz, timestamp, timestamptz, interval and oid are notable gaps, so a driver that binds these in binary (rather than as text) will fail.</li>
  <li>The COPY sub-protocol (COPY FROM STDIN / COPY TO STDOUT) is not implemented.</li>
  <li>MOVE and FETCH always report a row count of 0, rather than the number of rows actually moved or fetched.</li>
</ul>

